{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052137-umbra","id":1052137,"title":"Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-20T13:09:24-08:00","id":1052137,"title":"Umbra","content":"I hope you're all having a good day.<br /> So, was wondering, is it possible for a mage to meditate and/or collect quintessence in the spirit world faster and/or more efficient than it is in the skinlands/physical world?<br /> Also as far as I know there's no paradox in umbra, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:59:34-08:00","id":1052172,"title":"","content":"Not faster and not more efficient.<br /> <br /> Paradox exists, but magick is pretty much always coincidental. So you are safe if you don't botch...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:47:31-08:00","id":1052741,"title":"","content":"I can't see how going to the umbra would get you quintessence any faster and more efficiently than hanging around a powerful node or traveling from node to node that you have access to by virtue of your tradition. Any particular method you are referring to? Maybe transforming stuff into quintessence or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:55:57-08:00","id":1052804,"title":"","content":"I think if you have enough Prime to manage that, you can do it on either side of the gauntlet. Maybe safer on the other side, but I'd imagine the same speed and efficiency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:16:12-08:00","id":1052818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052137-umbra?p=1052804#post1052804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if you have enough Prime to manage that, you can do it on either side of the gauntlet. Maybe safer on the other side, but I'd imagine the same speed and efficiency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Safer? How many spirits are going to stand idly by while you start siphoning off their power? If the node is in a natural place, you can bet a Naturae is going to be angry about that, while it's it's more urban, there will certainly be a Pattern Spider or two who would try and stop you. Not to mention what would happen if a pack of Garou happen to spot you in the act?<br /> <br /> If you're going to meditate, that might be a bit better, but then you'll be spending about 30 minutes to an hour in the spirit world. You better hope something nasty isn't going to try and worm their way into your body, or leach off the power you're trying to absorb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:17:44-08:00","id":1052821,"title":"","content":"2 things:<br /> <br /> The Umbra may or may not have more Nodes than Earth, but it likely has more Tass. However a given kind of Tass might be the food of one or more Umbrood races. Tread carefully.<br /> <br /> Also as per the Spirit Kiss rote, sime Umbrood can give you Quintessence if you have enough Prime (2 or 3). Usually they will want something in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:23:04-08:00","id":1052828,"title":"","content":"I was referring to spacecat's &quot;transforming stuff into quintessence&quot; part, which was a Prime 4 effect that works instantaneously if I recall correctly. I assume it would be distintegrating slumbering, non-sentient spirits of objects and absorbing the raw quintessence they were made of when used on the other side of the gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:07:09-08:00","id":1052915,"title":"","content":"So, hypothetically speaking, let's say 1) I pierce the gauntlet, 2) &quot;eat&quot; the spirit that may or may not be protecting the place by turning it into quintessence, after which weaker spirits will probably flee, then 3) &quot;eat&quot; the spirit matter in the area, then jump back before something really big and scary finds me (With the blessing of a powerful rival spirit maybe so I don't gain the eternal emnity of spirits in general or at least am not the only one who experiences reprisal)... How long would that ideally take and How much Quintessence would I have gained?<br /> <br /> Compare to using Forces and Prime and transforming electrical power taken from an industrial grade power distributor transformer into a steady stream of quintessence (ideally with the address registered as a factory or something and with other measures to ensure the technocracy doesn't notice me), how much Quintessence will that likely get? Actually, how do I figure this second option out?<br /> <br /> Are there any variables that need to be worked out or established by the storyteller here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T20:29:21-08:00","id":1054176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052137-umbra?p=1052915#post1052915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, hypothetically speaking, let's say 1) I pierce the gauntlet, 2) &amp;quot;eat&amp;quot; the spirit that may or may not be protecting the place by turning it into quintessence, after which weaker spirits will probably flee, then 3) &amp;quot;eat&amp;quot; the spirit matter in the area, then jump back before something really big and scary finds me (With the blessing of a powerful rival spirit maybe so I don't gain the eternal emnity of spirits in general or at least am not the only one who experiences reprisal)... How long would that ideally take and How much Quintessence would I have gained?<br /> <br /> Compare to using Forces and Prime and transforming electrical power taken from an industrial grade power distributor transformer into a steady stream of quintessence (ideally with the address registered as a factory or something and with other measures to ensure the technocracy doesn't notice me), how much Quintessence will that likely get? Actually, how do I figure this second option out?<br /> <br /> Are there any variables that need to be worked out or established by the storyteller here?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 quintessence per point of essence of the spirit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T02:10:15-08:00","id":1054236,"title":"","content":"For sucking quint from the grid I would go for either Prime 4 to dissolve the Pattern of the electrical power, or Forces 3/ Prime 3 to transform the power into quint.<br /> 1 Quint per success and the necessity of a coverage for the huge amount of kWh needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T05:12:33-08:00","id":1054270,"title":"","content":"So I'm guessing a quick 1 scene raid will get you an amount of quint equal to the spirit's, plus a bit more from the consumption of spirit matter. I'm guessing this will net around less than 30 Quintessence in a scene at the risk of death and with the chance of getting a significantly smaller amount or a much smaller chance of getting more than this. (The smaller spirits seem to have 20 to 25 and are liable to spend some of it fighting you)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T05:20:38-08:00","id":1054273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052137-umbra?p=1054236#post1054236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sucking quint from the grid I would go for either Prime 4 to dissolve the Pattern of the electrical power, or Forces 3/ Prime 3 to transform the power into quint.<br /> 1 Quint per success and the necessity of a coverage for the huge amount of kWh needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm guessing a starting character will get around 10ish successes after a few hours of work casting the quintessence collecting spell, spending maybe 5 successes on Duration and 5 on getting Quintessence, this will net you 5 Quintessence per what time increment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T05:47:18-08:00","id":1054276,"title":"","content":"Sorry to jump in with a question, but it seems related. Can anyone advise where I might find more information about Paradox Spirits? Where they dwell, their nature, etc. I recall reading something - I think Masters of the Art a while ago - but haven't seen much else since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T06:39:04-08:00","id":1054285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052137-umbra?p=1054273#post1054273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I'm guessing a starting character will get around 10ish successes after a few hours of work casting the quintessence collecting spell, spending maybe 5 successes on Duration and 5 on getting Quintessence, this will net you 5 Quintessence per what time increment?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want a duration I would use damage over time for the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T06:54:45-08:00","id":1054292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone advise where I might find more information about Paradox Spirits? Where they dwell, their nature, etc. I recall reading something - I think Masters of the Art a while ago - but haven't seen much else since.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Basics of Revised and 2\u00ba ed have some. Then in the old Book of Madness (not the Revised one) there was a big section about Paradox with spirits (and a diferent clasification than Revised). The Book of Worlds has a section about paradox Relams and some spirits. There's less info about them in modern books that one would think (but I hope than in future M20 books we will have some sections and new stuff about them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:57:52-08:00","id":1054430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052137-umbra?p=1054285#post1054285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want a duration I would use damage over time for the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm trying to make a running effect that regularly collects quintessence (Into a periapt or something maybe). But if I can't do that, it means, I'm stuck with a several hours long ritual that would get me around 1 or 2 Quintessence per hour assuming I don't screw it up. This kinda looks like the rate of collection for a near starting character.<br /> <br /> So, for characters of similar build, risking life and limb in the spirit world could get you around maybe 20 to 30 quintessence with a big chance of dying or of becoming a target for hostile spirits (and maybe even suffering a fate worse than death) while the &quot;gathering it from electricity&quot; method gives you a steady stream of 1 or 2 an hour for several hours in a much safer manner I guess.<br /> <br /> So is there any way to get at an effect that regularly collects quintessence while I'm not manning it that isn't a Wonder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T14:51:34-08:00","id":1054471,"title":"","content":"If it where <b>that</b> easy, then Nodes wouldn't be worth the trouble.<br /> <br /> And everyone and their dogs would do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T16:49:14-08:00","id":1054506,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> <br /> Looking at the stealing Quintessence from the Umbra method more closely, I find that it would run a bit more like this:<br /> <br /> You'd need to spend several hours to build up dome Prime 3 + Spirit 3 effect to keep you from being killed by the spirit. Something to last the day and still have enough successes to give you a reasonable amount of safety. Then you'd probably want to cast a rite to enchant your mystic katana, or whatever weapon you have, for a scene so that the damage it deals to the spirits essence is fed to you in the form of quintessence. Then, assuming you confront something like a Jaggling that doesn't run away, you'd probably get Quintessence of 30 at best, but more likely something like 15 or less if it runs off or spends essence during the fight. Then you'd have maybe 5 minutes (a rite with 2 rolls?) to eat the substance of the spirit world and collect maybe 3 more Quintessence before you risk something else coming along and finding you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T17:24:49-08:00","id":1054523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052137-umbra?p=1054471#post1054471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it where <b>that</b> easy, then Nodes wouldn't be worth the trouble.<br /> <br /> And everyone and their dogs would do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even a wonder requiring arete 4, Prime 4, &amp; Forces 2 would likely only get you maybe 2 Quint per hour, and cost over 20 Quintessence to create to begin with. Not to mention it'll likely consume 3% of the Doel Nuclear Powerplant's hourly capacity (1.025*10<sup>9</sup> Joules per second according to some guy on the net) assuming a lightning bolt can be made from nothing using one point of Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T01:39:29-08:00","id":1055134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1052137-umbra?p=1054523#post1054523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And even a wonder requiring arete 4, Prime 4, &amp; Forces 2 would likely only get you maybe 2 Quint per hour, and cost over 20 Quintessence to create to begin with. Not to mention it'll likely consume 3% of the Doel Nuclear Powerplant's hourly capacity (1.025*10<sup>9</sup> Joules per second according to some guy on the net) assuming a lightning bolt can be made from nothing using one point of Quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum... That's a good amount... And I tell you, it IS worthed (I assume the Technocracy would keep several hidden nuclear powerplants connected to their Primal Batteries (Periapts) to collect the raw etherial energies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}